//
// A VARIANT CAST NEEDING A DEFAULT OF A BARE ENUM FIELD IS REFUSED (`@FR-D-NoEnumF` crossed with
// `@FR-N-Cast`).  N-Cast: `as τ` is an ASSERTION, refused at compile time where it cannot be
// kept; a cast to a variant answers the variant with every field at its default when the value
// holds another (@C131).  D-NoEnumF: a bare enum field without `= expr` has NO default — "the two
// places the domain STOPS" — and the partiality "is a TYPE rule … in the same family as (N-Cast)'s
// provable-fit requirement".  So `s as Tinted`, whose `tint: Colour` has no default, is refused,
// naming both cures (a field default, `Colour?`) and both safe spellings (`is` first, `as V?`).
// The D-NoEnumF cells beside this one measure a literal and `x?`; this one is the cast.
//
// @EXPECT_ERROR: record `Tinted` has no default: field `tint: NcColour` is an enum with no explicit choice
//
// @falsified-at: none — a conformance guard; the refusal fires on 18594597b, interpret and native.
// CHANNEL: the compile diagnostic.
// ARMED: no instrument.
// WITNESS: the diagnostic names the record, the field and the cures.
// HOLDS: `a-variant-cast-takes-the-default-its-fields-choose` beside it.

enum NcColour { Red, Green }
enum NcSh { Tinted { tint: NcColour, x: integer }, Plain { x: integer } }

fn main() {
  s: NcSh = Plain { x: 3 };
  w = s as Tinted;
  assert(w.x == 0, "unreachable");
}
